# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions (Synology disk + transfer safety)
#
# Keep this list LIMITED to confirmed non-build inputs. The Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .` then `pnpm install` / package builds / migrations — do NOT exclude
# workspace packages, lockfiles, migrations/, lib/db/, scripts/, version.json,
# docker/, tests, or other runtime/build assets.
#
# Note: bare globs like *.zip only match the context root in the classic
# builder; use **/ for nested paths.
# =============================================================================

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.cache
**/.turbo
**/.expo
**/.expo-shared
**/.replit-artifact

# Git metadata — but NOT the refs. scripts/build-identity.mjs resolves the commit
# an image was really built from out of .git/HEAD + .git/refs, because GIT_COMMIT
# arrives from .env and only deploy-synology.sh refreshes .env, so a Container
# Manager rebuild re-stamps NEW code with the OLD SHA. Objects, config and index
# stay excluded: a build needs to name its commit, not to replay its history.
# `!.git/refs/**` is spelled out beside `!.git/refs` because the two builder
# generations differ on whether re-including a directory re-includes its children;
# scripts/buildIdentity.test.mjs pins all four lines, and a context that ends up
# without refs degrades to `identitySource: "build-arg-declared"` — which
# verify-deployed-identity.mjs refuses to report as a verified deploy.
.git/*
!.git/HEAD
!.git/refs
!.git/refs/**
!.git/packed-refs
.github

# IDE / local agent noise
.idea
.vscode
.local
.cursor
.cache

# Secrets / local env (never bake into images)
.env
.env.*

# Logs and OS junk (anywhere in the tree)
**/*.log
**/desktop.ini
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.bak
**/*~
**/*.tmp
**/*.temp
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Owner-confirmed non-product MRI report archive (Windows PC only)
mri-reports/

# Release bundles / exported archives (not pnpm/Docker build inputs)
releases/
project.tar.gz
project.zip
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.zip

# Docs already excluded historically (not required for image build)
attached_assets/screenshots
README-WINDOWS.md
DEPLOY.md
replit.md
.replit

# Quarantined Super Admin folders to keep docker builds trace-free
artifacts/super-admin-portal
__super_admin_quarantine
